OL,3,GNEWSAOwl pellets reveal thriving mammal
OL,4,Apopulation
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe eating habits of barn owls have
OL,7,Frevealed a wide and varied small mammal
OL,8,Fpopulation hiding and thriving in a
OL,9,Fnature reserve.
OL,11,FResearchers from the Mammal Society
OL,12,Fhave been analysing owl pellets found
OL,13,Fat the Royal Society for the Protection
OL,14,Fof Birds' (RSPB) Saltholme reserve near
OL,15,FMiddlesbrough.
OL,17,FThe pellets, which the birds cough up,
OL,18,Fcontain undigested food such as bones
OL,19,Fand fur which makes it easier to see
OL,20,Fwhich animals are making a home in the
OL,21,Farea north of the River Tees.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,394,390,260,160,0,100
